<section id="overture" class="overture">
    <h2>Overture</h2>
    <p><strong>Podium is:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>An e-reader for music scores</li>
        <li>100% browser-based, 100% open-source, 100% free</li>
        <li>No login, no onboarding, no file importing, just use it! No installation required</li>
        <li>Unique UI featuring a circular menu and multiple layouts</li>
        <li>Not a music library: works with PDF files stored locally or in the cloud</li>
        <li>Extensive annotation support</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>...that runs on:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Desktops, Laptops, Chromebooks, tablets, smartphones: anything with a browser!</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>...with input devices:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>S-Pen, Apple Pencil, USI styli, fingers and thumbs</li>
        <li>Mouse, track pad, keyboard, footpedal page turners</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>...and practice tools:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Metronome with animated conducting baton</li>
        <li>Piano keyboard with integrated tuner</li>
        <li>Audio/video recorder with instant replay</li>
        <li>Realistic stopwatch and clock</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>...url:</strong><br>
    <a href="https://studiop5.org/podium" target="_blank">https://studiop5.org/podium</a></p>
    <p style="font-size:.85em;color:#888;">Podium is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. See the <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0-standalone.html" target="_blank">license</a> for complete terms. Users are responsible for ensuring they have the right to use any score files opened in Podium.</p>
</section>

<section id="chapter-1">
    <h2>Chapter 1: Quick Start</h2>

    <p>Welcome to Podium! This Quick Start guide will get you up and running in minutes. For detailed information on any topic, follow the chapter references throughout.</p>

    <h3>Getting Started in 3 Steps:</h3>

    <h4>1. Open a Score</h4>
    <p>Launch Podium at <a href="https://studiop5.org/podium" target="_blank">https://studiop5.org/podium</a>. You'll see a circular menu on a gray background, and the Score cell is highlighted. Drag out from the Open cell to reveal the Open Panel. Select a storage location (Local, Google Drive, Dropbox, OneDrive, or Recent), then navigate to a PDF score and tap to open it.</p>

    <figure>
        <div class="video-container" onclick="playVideo(this)">
            <img src="assets/quickopen.jpg" alt="Opening a score">
            <div class="play-overlay"></div>
            <button class="close-video" onclick="closeVideo(event, this.parentElement)">&times;</button>
