    <p><a href="#chapter-5" class="chapter-link">See Chapter 5: Layout Ring</a> for detailed layout controls and settings</p>

    <h4>3. Navigate and Annotate</h4>
    <p><strong>Navigation:</strong> Tap, swipe, or fling score pages to turn them. Long-press anywhere on the background to summon the menu. To hide the menu, fling it to any corner or edge, or long-press its center grip to park it in the upper left corner.</p>

    <p><strong>Annotations:</strong> Tap the inner ring's Ink cell to add annotations. The outer ring shows tools for:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Edit:</strong> Move, resize, rotate any annotation</li>
        <li><strong>Pencil/Pen:</strong> Draw freehand or straight lines</li>
        <li><strong>Rastrum:</strong> Draw music staves</li>
        <li><strong>Text:</strong> Add text boxes</li>
        <li><strong>Symbols:</strong> Insert music notation symbols</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Activate any Ink tool by tapping, then tap or drag on the score to use it. Configure the tool by dragging the corresponding panel from its cell. <strong>Note:</strong> Most Ink tools automatically deactivate after a few seconds of inactivity, so you won't accidentally stay in annotation mode when navigating pages.</p>

