    <h3>Essential Interface Tips:</h3>

    <h4>The Circular Menu</h4>
    <p>The menu has three parts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Grip (center):</strong> Drag to move menu, tap to collapse/expand, long press or fling toward edges to park</li>
        <li><strong>Inner Ring:</strong> 6 cells (Score, Layout, Ink, Page, App, More) - tap to select</li>
        <li><strong>Outer Ring:</strong> Shows actions for the selected inner ring cell</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Both rings can be rotated by dragging them in a circular motion.</p>

    <figure>
        <div class="video-container" onclick="playVideo(this)">
            <img src="assets/quickmenu.jpg" alt="Circular menu">
            <div class="play-overlay"></div>
            <button class="close-video" onclick="closeVideo(event, this.parentElement)">&times;</button>
            <video controls controlsList="nofullscreen nodownload" disablePictureInPicture preload="none">
                <source src="assets/quickpanel.webm" type="video/webm">
                Your browser does not support the video tag.
            </video>
        </div>
        <figcaption>The circular menu showing Grip, Inner Ring, and Outer Ring</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p><a href="#chapter-3" class="chapter-link">See Chapter 3: Interface Basics</a> for complete interface details</p>

    <h4>Panels</h4>
    <p>Cells with small diamond-shaped pointers (like compass points) contain hidden panels. Drag out from these cells to reveal the panel. Once open, reposition panels by dragging their textured header. Hide a panel by flinging it from the header, or close them by tapping the &#x1F5D9 button.</p>

    <h4>Resizing and Moving</h4>
    <p>Everything in Podium—menu, panels, layouts—is resizable and movable using two-finger pinch-and-pan gestures (or Ctrl+mouse/Ctrl+wheel for desktop). <a href="#chapter-3" class="chapter-link">See Chapter 3: Interface Basics</a> for details.</p>

    <h4>Background Gestures:</h4>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Swipe left ⇄ right:</strong> Enter/exit full-screen (on iPhone/iPad, use the Screen button in the App Ring instead)</li>
        <li><strong>Swipe top ⇅ bottom:</strong> Reset and center menu</li>
        <li><strong>Long press:</strong> Summon menu to that location</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Saving Your Work</h3>
    <p>Tap the inner ring's Score cell, then tap Save (or drag out from Save to choose a new location/name). Your annotations and settings are saved within the PDF file.</p>

    <figure>
        <div class="video-container" onclick="playVideo(this)">
            <img src="assets/quicksave.jpg" alt="Save Panel">
            <div class="play-overlay"></div>
            <button class="close-video" onclick="closeVideo(event, this.parentElement)">&times;</button>
            <video controls controlsList="nofullscreen nodownload" disablePictureInPicture preload="none">
