    </figure>

    <p><a href="#chapter-4" class="chapter-link">See Chapter 4: Score Ring</a> for saving, printing, and score details</p>

    <h3>Managing Pages</h3>
    <p>To add, remove, or rearrange pages, tap the inner ring's Page cell. The outer ring provides:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Add:</strong>Insert blank pages</li>
        <li><strong>Delete:</strong>Remove pages from the score</li>
        <li><strong>Undo:</strong> Undo the last page operation</li>
        <li><strong>Copy/Paste:</strong> Rearrange or duplicate pages</li>
        <li><strong>Numbers:</strong> Configure page numbering and keyboard shortcuts</li>
        <li><strong>Merge:</strong> Convert annotations into permanent PDF content</li>
        <li><strong>Magnify:</strong> Zoom in on page details</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Note:</strong> Like Ink tools, Page tools auto-deactivate after a few seconds of inactivity.</p>

    <p>The page paste buffer is shared across all Podium tabs and windows, and persists across sessions. This lets you copy pages from one score and paste them into another, making it easy to assemble custom practice scores. Note that tabs of the web app (studiop5.org) share one paste buffer, and tabs of the browser extension share another — copying across these boundaries is not possible.</p>

